1
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:24,380
Champagne flutes on the limestone ledge

2
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:27,610
Three dozen stories above the avenue hedge

3
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:30,110
You’re leaning back in your linen shirt

4
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:34,820
Laughing too loud so the truth won't hurt

5
00:00:34,870 --> 00:00:39,010
The sun drops low like a minted coin

6
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:43,580
Where the rusted girders and brick adjoin

7
00:00:43,630 --> 00:00:46,130
Everyone’s acting like August stayed

8
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:50,210
While the terrace shadows begin to trade

9
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:54,370
There’s a sudden bite in the evening air

10
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:57,970
And you trace the rim of your crystal ware

11
00:00:58,020 --> 00:01:02,330
You look at the skyline, not at me

12
00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:06,070
Like a ship already out to sea

13
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:09,710
It’s copper on the terrace, gold turning to rust

14
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:14,030
All of our promises ground into velvet dust

15
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:17,790
Dance me to the edge of the balcony rail

16
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:22,070
Before the warm trade winds begin to fail

17
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:25,690
You’re holding my waist like a souvenir

18
00:01:25,740 --> 00:01:29,810
In the brightest hour of a dying year

19
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:36,060
Yeah, it’s copper on the terrace tonight

20
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:43,060
Your best friend’s spinning an old French record

21
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:46,830
Our history’s suddenly strangely checkered

22
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:50,550
You hand me your jacket, the lining’s torn

23
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:54,450
Swearing this fever is newly born

24
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:58,390
But I know the cadence of an exit line

25
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:02,330
Dressed up in vintage cabernet wine

26
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:06,370
You kiss my collarbone, quick and polite

27
00:02:06,420 --> 00:02:09,770
Beneath the amber Edison string-bulb light

28
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:13,310
There’s a sudden bite in the evening air

29
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:17,190
And you trace the rim of your crystal ware

30
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:21,530
You look at the skyline, not at me

31
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:26,000
Like a ship already out to sea

32
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:30,850
It’s copper on the terrace, gold turning to rust

33
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:35,050
All of our promises ground into velvet dust

34
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:38,930
Dance me to the edge of the balcony rail

35
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:43,150
Before the warm trade winds begin to fail

36
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:46,690
You’re holding my waist like a souvenir

37
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:51,540
In the brightest hour of a dying year

38
00:02:51,590 --> 00:02:58,220
Yeah, it’s copper on the terrace tonight

39
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:02,210
Remember July on the fire escape?

40
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:04,110
When every tomorrow had a reckless shape!

41
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:06,130
Now you’re folding your secrets into your cuff

42
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:08,190
As if wanting you once wasn't quite enough!

43
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:10,210
Don't tell me the season is just a phase

44
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:13,000
When I see the frost in your sideways gaze!

45
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:18,410
It’s copper on the terrace, gold turning to rust!

46
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:22,410
All of our promises ground into velvet dust!

47
00:03:22,460 --> 00:03:26,390
Dance me to the edge of the balcony rail

48
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:31,430
Before the warm trade winds begin to fail!

49
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:34,290
You’re holding my waist like a souvenir

50
00:03:34,340 --> 00:03:38,330
In the brightest hour of a dying year

51
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:45,160
Yeah, it’s copper on the terrace tonight!

52
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:50,930
Copper and rust on the avenue

53
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:55,050
The air turns sharp between me and you

54
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:58,480
Just a souvenir

55
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:03,530
in the fading glow
